<section class="section" id="licenses">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="grid grid-3">
      <div class="card"><h3>Engine: Apache-2.0</h3><p>The Python data-plane library both products import. Open source.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>CLI: BUSL-1.1</h3><p>Source-available. Free to use; the licence restricts offering it as a competing service. Converts to Apache-2.0 on its change date.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><h3>Platform: commercial</h3><p>Licensed per instance under the subscription. A licence key is recorded in the audit log; the product does not phone home.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Common questions</p>
      <h2>The honest answers</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details><summary>What counts as an instance?</summary><div class="faq-body">One deployment of the Platform: one Compose stack with its own database, serving one organisation. If you run separate dev, staging, and production deployments, each is an instance; the Enterprise tier prices them together.</div></details>
      <details><summary>Is the CLI really free?</summary><div class="faq-body">Yes. It is free to download and run, with every engine capability included. It is source-available under BUSL-1.1, which is not an OSI open-source licence; the restriction is on offering Decoy itself as a hosted service to others.</div></details>
      <details><summary>Is there a free trial of the Platform?</summary><div class="faq-body">Not a self-serve one. The CLI is the evaluation path for the engine; for the Platform we run scoped pilots. Write to us and we will set one up.</div></details>
      <details><summary>What does self-hosting cost me?</summary><div class="faq-body">A Linux host with at least 4 vCPU, 8 GB of RAM, and 50 GB of disk, plus Postgres storage that grows with your audit log. There is no hosted option.</div></details>
      <details><summary>Is Decoy certified for HIPAA, SOC 2, or PCI?</summary><div class="faq-body">No. Decoy holds no SOC 2 report and does not sign a BAA today. The Disguise templates and the compliance mapping on the <a href="/security/#compliance">security page</a> help teams preparing for those audits; they are not certifications.</div></details>
      <details><summary>Do you offer SAML?</summary><div class="faq-body">No. Single sign-on is OIDC, tested with Okta, Entra ID, Google Workspace, Keycloak, and Auth0. Identity providers that only speak SAML are not supported.</div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

